/-!
# Tag 0DXI: the cohomology of the derived completion of the sections on a punctured spectrum

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring, let `U = Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` be its punctured spectrum, let
`ℱ` be a coherent `𝒪_U`-module and let `I ⊆ A` be an ideal. [Stacks, Tag 0DXI] asserts

`Hⁱ(RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧) = lim_n Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`   for all `i`,

the completion on the left being the derived `I`-adic completion of the object `RΓ(U, ℱ)` of
`D(A)`. This file proves it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_toLimit_homology_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections` —
  **[Stacks, Tag 0DXI]**: the comparison map
  `Hⁱ(RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧) ⟶ lim_n Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` is an isomorphism, in every degree `i`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_homologyIso_limit_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections` —
  the same read as an isomorphism of `A`-modules, with the comparison map still pinned.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem_congr` — the tower `n ↦ ℱ/Iⁿℱ` of
  the right-hand side depends only on `I`, not on the finite generating family through which the
  sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U` is written down.

## What the left-hand side is

`RΓ(U, -)` is `Stacks.Algebraization.puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections`, the unbounded derived
`A`-linear sections of the punctured spectrum read as a ringed space, and `(-)^∧` is
`DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a` for a finite generating family `a` of `I` — the
derived completion along `Ideal.span {a_1, …, a_r} = I`, which is a reflection of `D(A)` onto the
objects derived complete along `I` by `DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletion_isReflection`, that is
the functor of [Stacks, Tag 0G3E]. The generating family is universally quantified and exists
because `A` is Noetherian; nothing about the completion is assumed.

In particular **no derived limit is taken as a hypothesis**. The earlier statements of
`PuncturedSpectrumCohomologyMittagLeffler.lean` name the left-hand side by an object `ℒ` carrying
an `IsDerivedLimit` hypothesis for the tower `ℱ/Iⁿℱ`; here that object is produced, and it is
produced together with the identification of `RΓ(U, ℒ)` with `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧`.

## The route

1. `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_isDerivedLimit_and_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedSections`
   produces one object `ℒ` of `D(𝒪_U)` which is a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ ℱ/Iⁿℱ` and
   whose derived sections are `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧`. That is [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] parts (3) and (4) followed
   by [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], with the two derived global-sections functors of this library
   identified. Its hypotheses hold here: the punctured spectrum of a Noetherian local ring is a
   quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, and `I𝒪_U` is generated by the global sections
   `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r`.
2. `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedSectionsOverBase.exists_shortExact_homology_derivedSectionsOver`
   turns the derived limit into the Milnor short exact sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0D60] for
   `Hⁱ(RΓ(U, ℒ))`.
3. Its `R¹lim` term vanishes because the inverse system `n ↦ H^{i-1}(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` is
   Mittag-Leffler in every degree, which is
   `Stacks.Algebraization`
   `.isMittagLefflerCategorical_puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem_of_quotientTower` — [Stacks,
   Tag 0DX1] part (2) in the positive degrees, and the degree-zero and negative-degree
   statements proved beside it.
4. The conclusion transports from `RΓ(U, ℒ)` to `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧` along the isomorphism of step 1: a
   distinguished triangle is carried to a distinguished triangle, and the comparison map to the
   limit is composed with the isomorphism on cohomology.

## Implementation notes

*The tower.* The inverse system of the right-hand side is the library's own
`Stacks.Algebraization.adicQuotientSystem` at the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U`, together
with the cokernel projections of `Stacks.Algebraization.adicQuotientCone`; it is constructed, not
characterized by hypotheses, so the three clauses that pinned it down in the earlier statements —
epimorphy of the projections, their compatibility with the transitions and the coherence of the
terms — are discharged here. Coherence is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isCoherent_adicQuotientSystem_obj`.

*The comparison map is pinned.* As in the earlier statements the map shown invertible is
characterized by its composites with the limit projections through a morphism
`α : RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ ∏ₙ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` which is itself required to exhibit `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧` as a derived
limit of `n ↦ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`, by fitting into the Milnor triangle of that system. A bare
existential would be weaker than the source.

*The two coherence predicates.* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` and
`SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` are the two spellings of coherence this subtree carries, bridged by
`AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent` and its converse; the
statement is given in the first, which is the one the Mittag-Leffler input of
`PuncturedSpectrumCohomologyMittagLeffler.lean` uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D60](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D60)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DX1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DX1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G3E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G3E)

## Tags

local cohomology, punctured spectrum, derived completion, formal geometry
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedSectionsOverBase

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] modulesEnoughInjectives

-- `HasDerivedCategory.standard` at a raised priority. The library also carries the global
-- instance `StacksDraft.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall.hasDerivedCategory`, which names the
-- derived category of sheaves of modules at the hom universe `u` rather than `u + 1`; the
-- statements this file consumes are all at `u + 1`, so the standard instance has to win.
attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Punctured

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]

/-- **The punctured spectrum of a Noetherian local ring as a scheme.** This is the open subscheme
`Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` whose ringed space is `Stacks.Algebraization.puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace`. -/
abbrev puncturedSpectrumScheme : Scheme.{u} := (Stacks.puncturedSpectrum A).toScheme

/-- **The sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U` on the punctured spectrum**: the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
generated by the images of `a_1, …, a_r` under `A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`. It is
`Stacks.Algebraization.koszulIdealSheafData` at those global sections, the extension to `U` of the
ideal they span. -/
abbrev puncturedSpectrumIdealSheaf {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A) :
    (puncturedSpectrumScheme A).IdealSheafData :=
  koszulIdealSheafData (puncturedSpectrumScheme A)
    (structureGenerators (puncturedSpectrumScheme A) A (puncturedSpectrumScalars A) a)

/-- **The tower `n ↦ ℱ/Iⁿℱ` on the punctured spectrum**, the inverse system whose limit of
cohomology is the right-hand side of [Stacks, Tag 0DXI]: the library's canonical adic quotient
tower at the sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U`. -/
abbrev puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A)) :=
  adicQuotientSystem (puncturedSpectrumIdealSheaf A a) F

end Punctured

section Main

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]

/-- The derived category of `A`-modules has products indexed by `ℕ`. -/
noncomputable local instance derivedCategoryModuleCatProductsNat :
    HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) :=
  Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_derivedCategory

variable (I : Ideal A)
  (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A)))
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F] {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A)

/-- The adic quotient tower of a coherent module on the punctured spectrum has coherent terms.
This is `Stacks.Algebraization.isCoherent_adicQuotientSystem_obj`, read in the coherence
predicate the Mittag-Leffler statements of `PuncturedSpectrumCohomologyMittagLeffler.lean`
use. -/
theorem stacksIsCoherent_puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem_obj (n : ℕᵒᵖ) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent ((puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem A a F).obj n) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.stacksIsCoherent_of_isCoherent
    (@isCoherent_adicQuotientSystem_obj (puncturedSpectrumScheme A) _
      (puncturedSpectrumIdealSheaf A a) F
      (AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent (M := F) ‹_›) n)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] [SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F] in
/-- **The tower of the right-hand side depends only on the ideal `I`.** Two finite families of
`A` spanning the same ideal give the same sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U`, hence the same adic quotient
tower; so the inverse system `n ↦ ℱ/Iⁿℱ` of [Stacks, Tag 0DXI] is determined by `I` and not by
the presentation of `I` through which it is written down. -/
theorem puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem_congr {s : ℕ} (b : Fin s → A)
    (hab : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = Ideal.span (Set.range b)) :
    puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem A a F = puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem A b F :=
  congrArg (fun 𝓘 ↦ adicQuotientSystem 𝓘 F)
    (koszulIdealSheafData_structureGenerators_congr (puncturedSpectrumScheme A) A
      (puncturedSpectrumScalars A) a b hab)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0DXI.** Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring, let
`U = Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` be its punctured spectrum, let `ℱ` be a coherent `𝒪_U`-module and let
`I ⊆ A` be an ideal, presented by a finite generating family `a_1, …, a_r`. Then for every `i`
the comparison map

`Hⁱ(RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧) ⟶ lim_n Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`

is an isomorphism, where `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧` is the derived `I`-adic completion of `RΓ(U, ℱ)` in `D(A)`
and `ℱ/Iⁿℱ` is the adic quotient tower at the sheaf of ideals `I𝒪_U`.

The comparison map is the one determined by the Milnor triangle: it is characterized by its
composites with the limit projections through a morphism
`α : RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ ∏ₙ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` which is required to exhibit `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧` as a derived limit
of `n ↦ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`, so the conclusion is about the comparison map and not about some map.

Nothing is assumed: the derived limit of the tower, the identification of its derived sections
with `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧` and the Mittag-Leffler condition that makes the comparison invertible are all
produced — by [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] parts (3) and (4), by [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], and by
[Stacks, Tag 0DX1] part (2) together with its degree-zero and negative-degree companions. -/
@[stacks 0DXI "the whole lemma: for `(A, 𝔪)` Noetherian local with punctured spectrum `U`, a \
coherent `𝒪_U`-module `ℱ` and an ideal `I ⊆ A`, the comparison map \
`Hⁱ(RΓ(U,ℱ)^∧) ⟶ lim_n Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` is an isomorphism in every degree `i`, the left-hand side \
being the derived `I`-adic completion in `D(A)` of the derived sections `RΓ(U,ℱ)` and the tower \
on the right being the adic quotient tower at `I𝒪_U`. The map shown invertible is the comparison \
map, characterized by the limit projections through an `α` required to exhibit `RΓ(U,ℱ)^∧` as a \
derived limit of `n ↦ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`"]
theorem isIso_toLimit_homology_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections
    (ha : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I) (i : ℤ) :
    let S := puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem A a F
    let Hi := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i
    let C := (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a).obj
      ((puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections A).obj ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) 0).obj F))
    let RΓS : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
      S ⋙ DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) 0 ⋙
        puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections A
    let Y : ℕ → DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) := fun n ↦ RΓS.obj (op n)
    let d : (∏ᶜ Y) ⟶ ∏ᶜ Y := Pi.lift fun n : ℕ ↦
      Pi.π Y n - Pi.π Y (n + 1) ≫ RΓS.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op
    ∃ (α : C ⟶ ∏ᶜ Y) (β : (∏ᶜ Y) ⟶ C⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk α d β ∈ distTriang (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) ∧
      ∃ q : Hi.obj C ⟶ limit (puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem A S i),
        (∀ n : ℕ, q ≫ limit.π (puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem A S i) (op n) =
          Hi.map α ≫ Hi.map (Pi.π Y n)) ∧ IsIso q := by
  intro S Hi C RΓS Y d
  -- `ha` fixes the ideal the tower is taken along; the tower itself is the library's own
  have _ : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I := ha
  have hFc := AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent (M := F) ‹_›
  -- step 1: one object is both a derived limit of the tower and the completion of the sections
  obtain ⟨L, ⟨hprod, hL⟩, ⟨θ⟩⟩ :=
    @exists_isDerivedLimit_and_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedSections
      (puncturedSpectrumScheme A) _ _ A _ (puncturedSpectrumScalars A) r a F hFc
  have := hprod
  -- the derived sections of the punctured spectrum, at this file's spelling of the ringed space
  have θ' : (puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections A).obj L ≅ C := θ
  -- step 2: the Milnor short exact sequence of the derived limit
  obtain ⟨α₀, β₀, hT₀, hdata⟩ := exists_shortExact_homology_derivedSectionsOver
    (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A) (puncturedSpectrumScalars A)
    (S ⋙ DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) 0) L hL
  obtain ⟨e, incl, q₀, w, -, -, hq₀, hshort⟩ := hdata i
  -- step 3: the `R¹lim` term vanishes, in every degree
  have hML := isMittagLefflerCategorical_puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem_of_quotientTower A F S
    (stacksIsCoherent_puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem_obj A F a)
    (fun n ↦ (adicQuotientCone (puncturedSpectrumIdealSheaf A a) F).π.app n)
    (fun _ ↦ coequalizer.π_epi)
    (fun {_ _} h ↦ (adicQuotientCone (puncturedSpectrumIdealSheaf A a) F).w h) (i - 1)
  have hepi := epi_milnorDifference_of_isMittagLefflerCategorical
    (puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem A S (i - 1)) hML
  have hincl : incl = 0 :=
    ((Preadditive.epi_iff_isZero_cokernel _).1 hepi).eq_of_src _ _
  have : Mono q₀ := hshort.exact.mono_g hincl
  have : Epi q₀ := hshort.epi_g
  have : IsIso q₀ := isIso_of_mono_of_epi _
  -- step 4: transport the conclusion along `θ : RΓ(U, ℒ) ≅ RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧`
  refine ⟨θ'.inv ≫ α₀, β₀ ≫ (shiftFunctor (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (1 : ℤ)).map θ'.hom,
    ?_, Hi.map θ'.inv ≫ q₀, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact isomorphic_distinguished _ hT₀ _
      (Triangle.isoMk _ _ θ'.symm (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (by simp [Triangle.mk])
        (by simp only [Triangle.mk_mor₂, Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id, Category.id_comp]; rfl)
        (by simp [Triangle.mk]))
  · intro n
    exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun z ↦ Hi.map θ'.inv ≫ z) (hq₀ n)).trans
        ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
          (congrArg (fun z ↦ z ≫ Hi.map (Pi.π Y n)) (Hi.map_comp θ'.inv α₀).symm)))
  · have : IsIso (Hi.map θ'.inv) := inferInstance
    infer_instance

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0DXI, read as an isomorphism of `A`-modules.** In the situation of
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_toLimit_homology_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections`, the
degree-`i` cohomology of the derived `I`-adic completion of `RΓ(U, ℱ)` is isomorphic to the
inverse limit of the `A`-modules `Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`.

The isomorphism keeps the characterization by the limit projections and `α` is still required to
be a derived-limit structure map of `n ↦ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`, so what is asserted is that the
comparison map is invertible and not merely that the two modules are abstractly isomorphic. -/
@[stacks 0DXI "the whole lemma read as an isomorphism of `A`-modules: \
`Hⁱ(RΓ(U,ℱ)^∧) ≅ lim_n Hⁱ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` in every degree `i`, for `(A, 𝔪)` Noetherian local with \
punctured spectrum `U`, a coherent `𝒪_U`-module `ℱ` and an ideal `I ⊆ A`. The isomorphism is the \
comparison map, characterized by the limit projections through an `α` required to exhibit \
`RΓ(U,ℱ)^∧` as a derived limit of `n ↦ RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)`"]
theorem exists_homologyIso_limit_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections
    (ha : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I) (i : ℤ) :
    let S := puncturedSpectrumAdicQuotientSystem A a F
    let Hi := DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i
    let C := (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a).obj
      ((puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections A).obj ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) 0).obj F))
    let RΓS : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
      S ⋙ DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (puncturedSpectrumRingedSpace A))) 0 ⋙
        puncturedSpectrumDerivedSections A
    let Y : ℕ → DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) := fun n ↦ RΓS.obj (op n)
    let d : (∏ᶜ Y) ⟶ ∏ᶜ Y := Pi.lift fun n : ℕ ↦
      Pi.π Y n - Pi.π Y (n + 1) ≫ RΓS.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)).op
    ∃ (α : C ⟶ ∏ᶜ Y) (β : (∏ᶜ Y) ⟶ C⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk α d β ∈ distTriang (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) ∧
      ∃ eq : Hi.obj C ≅ limit (puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem A S i),
        ∀ n : ℕ, eq.hom ≫ limit.π (puncturedSpectrumCohomologySystem A S i) (op n) =
          Hi.map α ≫ Hi.map (Pi.π Y n) := by
  intro S Hi C RΓS Y d
  obtain ⟨α, β, hT, q, hq, hiso⟩ :=
    isIso_toLimit_homology_derivedCompletion_puncturedSpectrumSections A I F a ha i
  exact ⟨α, β, hT, asIso q, hq⟩

end Main

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
